## What went wrong

The only real compile error was in `ErpSyncFinalizer`: the qualified reference `System.QUEUEABLE_NEW_CHAIN` does not resolve in this org ("Variable does not exist: System"), and because the two classes reference each other, that error invalidated `ErpAccountSyncJob` and the hidden test class as well.

**Fixes applied**

1. **Removed the chain constant.** The retry is now enqueued with the single‑argument `System.enqueueJob(job)`, which is always available and starts the retry in its own chain (so a failed chain cannot swallow the retry). No `System.<CONSTANT>` reference is used anymore.
2. **Kept `System.attachFinalizer(...)`** (that call compiles – it was never the failing expression) and made sure it is the very first statement of `execute`, so every run is logged.
3. **Simplified the DML.** Instead of querying and updating (which silently skips an Account that no longer exists and would wrongly report "Success"), the job builds the `Account` records from the Ids and issues **one single `update` statement**. A single DML statement is atomic, so if any record cannot be saved an uncaught `DmlException` rolls the whole transaction back – none of the changes are kept and the finalizer sees the failure, logs it and schedules the next attempt.

