/**
 * Creates Accounts together with their Contacts.
 *
 * Design notes
 * ------------
 * - All writes go through a single fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork that is created inside the
 *   method and committed exactly once with commitWork(). This class never issues DML.
 * - The unit of work infers the SObject types from the records that are registered with
 *   it, so it is created with its no-argument constructor.
 * - The parent/child link is expressed by assigning the parent Account *instance* to the
 *   Contact.Account relationship field. The unit of work inserts the parents first and
 *   resolves the Contact.AccountId foreign key from the newly created Account before the
 *   children are inserted, so a single commit is enough and no extra round trip (or hand
 *   written DML) is required.
 * - Bulk safe: the library performs one INSERT per SObject type, so hundreds of Accounts
 *   and Contacts are handled within the normal DML limits. There is no SOQL and no DML
 *   inside a loop.
 */
public with sharing class AccountOnboardingService {

    /**
     * Creates one Account for every entry of the map (named after the map key) and one
     * Contact for every last name of the matching list. Every Contact is linked to the
     * Account created for the same map entry.
     *
     * @param contactLastNamesByAccountName Map of Account Name -> list of Contact Last
     *                                        Names. A null value or an empty list simply
     *                                        means the Account is created without
     *                                        Contacts.
     * @return The Accounts that were created, with their Ids populated. An empty list is
     *         returned (and nothing is written) when the incoming map is null or empty.
     */
    public static List<Account> createAccountsWithContacts(Map<String, List<String>> contactLastNamesByAccountName) {
        List<Account> createdAccounts = new List<Account>();

        // Nothing to do: return an empty list and write nothing.
        if (contactLastNamesByAccountName == null || contactLastNamesByAccountName.isEmpty()) {
            return createdAccounts;
        }

        // A single unit of work for the whole operation -> a single commit and a single
        // transaction for all the Accounts and Contacts.
        fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork unitOfWork = new fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork();

        List<Account> accountsToCreate = new List<Account>();
        List<Contact> contactsToCreate = new List<Contact>();

        for (String accountName : contactLastNamesByAccountName.keySet()) {
            // Account.Name is required; skip meaningless entries instead of failing the
            // whole transaction (which would otherwise discard every other record).
            if (String.isBlank(accountName)) {
                continue;
            }

            Account account = new Account(Name = accountName);
            accountsToCreate.add(account);

            List<String> contactLastNames = contactLastNamesByAccountName.get(accountName);
            if (contactLastNames == null) {
                continue;
            }

            for (String contactLastName : contactLastNames) {
                // Contact.LastName is required.
                if (String.isBlank(contactLastName)) {
                    continue;
                }

                Contact contact = new Contact(LastName = contactLastName);
                // Link the Contact to its parent by instance: the unit of work resolves
                // Contact.AccountId from the Id of the newly created Account on commit.
                contact.Account = account;
                contactsToCreate.add(contact);
            }
        }

        // Nothing valid to create -> do not touch the database at all.
        if (accountsToCreate.isEmpty()) {
            return createdAccounts;
        }

        // Register the parents first so that the unit of work can resolve the foreign
        // keys of the children before inserting them.
        for (Account account : accountsToCreate) {
            unitOfWork.registerNew(account);
        }
        for (Contact contact : contactsToCreate) {
            unitOfWork.registerNew(contact);
        }

        // Single commit: Accounts and Contacts are written together. Errors raised by the
        // unit of work are intentionally not swallowed so that failures are never reported
        // as success.
        unitOfWork.commitWork();

        // The Ids have been populated on the very same Account instances by the insert.
        createdAccounts.addAll(accountsToCreate);
        return createdAccounts;
    }
}
```

The failure was the unit-of-work class name: in fflib-apex-common the unit of work class is `fflib_UoW` (not `fflib_UnitOfWork`), and `Application.UnitOfWork.newInstance()` returns an `fflib_UoW`. Everything else stays the same: the Opportunity updates and the `Deal_Won__e` events are registered on that single unit of work, and `commitWork()` performs the DML first and only publishes the events after the DML has succeeded (a failed save rolls back and the exception propagates).

