## What was fixed

The custom metadata records were rejected because the Metadata CRUD API (used by the current `sf` CLI when deploying custom metadata) requires the `fullName` attribute on the root `<CustomMetadata>` element. Each metadata file now carries `fullName` matching its record's developer name, and the trigger action records point at the existing `sObject_Trigger_Setting__mdt` record using the qualified metadata type reference `sObject_Trigger_Setting__mdt.Opportunity`.

The Apex was also hardened so that the finalizer is safe whichever entry point the framework uses (`TriggerAction.DmlFinalizer.execute` or `FinalizerHandler.handleDynamicFinalizers`): both paths go through the same *drain* of the buffer, so exactly one `OpportunityErpSyncJob` is enqueued per DML operation (and none at all when the buffer is empty).

